        <body>
            <div xml:id="d636">

                <pb facs="0532" n="450" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg450"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/1093.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Mexican Chargé
                        d’Affaires.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-04-07"><hi rendition="#italic">April 7,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 447.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of the embassy’s note of the 26th ultimo, stating that the governor of Sonora
                    has reported that armed bands have invaded that State from its northern
                    boundary, and communicating to the Department a request of your Government that
                    steps be taken to prevent the movement of such armed groups toward Mexican
                    territory.</p>
                <p>Copies of your note have been sent to the War Department and the Department of
                    Justice.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.],</p>
                <closer>(For <signed>Mr. Knox</signed>.)<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Huntington Wilson</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
